{{Quote|Stay focused, there's a Heavy Unit approaching.|[[Lotus]]}}<section begin=intro />'''Eximus''' (version 2.0), also known as '''Heavy Units''', are a category of special elite variants of standard enemies introduced in {{ver|12.0}} and reworked in {{ver|31.5}} that can appear in any mission type. They come in several varieties, each with unique abilities (some of which are similar to [[Tenno]] abilities) and are usually much stronger than an average member of their [[Factions|faction]], although effects vary from type to type. Compared to normal units, Eximus have increased stats, resistances, and possession of {{D|Overguard}}, posing a reasonable challenge for under-equipped or inexperienced Tenno.<section end="intro" />
==Overview==
Eximus are normal enemies that have been empowered with special abilities, while their visuals and audio cues have been amplified to make them stand out amongst their peers. Their durability has been dramatically increased in the form of {{D|Overguard}}, a special health buffer that renders them immune to most crowd control until removed. Overall, Eximus pose a significant threat to Tenno, making them high priority targets.

Eximus units drop 500-750 {{Resource|Credits}} , and provide an additional 1,000 base [[Affinity]] gain over their normal counterpart (before level scaling calculations). Eximus units above level 30 also have a chance to drop a {{Resource|Riven Sliver}}, with those in [[The Steel Path]] having the same drop chance. They are also guaranteed to drop one [[Energy Orb]], two [[Health Orb]]s, and either [[Pickups#Ammo|Primary Ammo]] or [[Pickups#Ammo|Secondary Ammo]] on death. This is in addition to the enemies normal chance to drop orbs and ammo, and is unaffected by additional loot effects. Eximus spawn at the same level as other enemy units.

Eximus will normally start appearing only after '''60''' seconds have elapsed in the mission and only up to '''5''' Eximus units can be present simultaneously. These limits do not apply in some missions or when some modifiers are in effect. Eximus units are plentiful:

* every third wave of [[Defense]] missions
* in [[Sortie]] missions with the Eximus Stronghold condition
* in [[Razorback Armada]] assassinations
* towards the end of [[Abyssal Zone]] missions
* in [[Operation: Belly of the Beast]] alerts and in its version of the [[Brutus]] node ([[Ascension]])
* in the [[Undercroft]] when using the 3 bonus portals
* in [[Netracells]], also subject to equipped Keyglyphs
* in [[Archimedea]] missions, also subject to deviations and risk variables in effect
* in [[Höllvania]] missions, also subject to the current season
* in [[Descendia]] Infernums with the Eximus Cabal penance

==Eximus Types==
Almost any base unit type ([[Osprey]], [[Lancer]], [[MOA]], etc.) can spawn as an Eximus, though certain units can only spawn as a particular Eximus type, e.g. [[Charger]]s can only spawn as Parasitic Types. They can easily be identified by their special auras and larger sizes, and frequently have unique textures/skins to make them more visually distinctive.

{{Faction|Sentient}} and {{Faction|Wild}} are the only factions that do not have Eximus units.

===Arctic / Cryonic / Frozen===
[[File:ArcticEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Arctic Eximus]]
'''Arctic''', '''Cryonic''', or '''Frozen''' Eximus units generate a {{A|Snow Globe}}-like barrier with '''10,000''' [[Damage/Object|object]]-based health that lasts for '''20''' seconds. This barrier appears as a white/blue transparent sphere and will follow the Eximus. The barrier protects all units inside from ranged attacks and area of effects. Players inside the barrier become afflicted with {{D|Cold}} status effect every second, but all stacks are removed upon leaving the barrier. Due to the barrier's object-based health, it is not affected by [[Critical Hit|critical]] damage, meaning crit-focused weapons are less effective than raw damage weapons. Barrier health does not scale with enemy level.

All factions can become Arctic Eximus. [[Infested]] are referred to as Frozen. [[Rogue_Culverin#Variants|Elementa Culverins]] are referred to as Cryonic, and possess a unique mortar attack that leaves a lingering cloud of {{D|Cold}}, which will inflict a {{D|Cold}} proc to anyone inside it.

In [[Höllvania]], Arctic Eximus are significantly more common in the [[Höllvania#Weather|Winter season]].
{{clr}}

===Arson===
[[File:ArsonEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Arson Eximus]]
'''Arson''' Eximus units have the ability to release a '''30''' meter radius {{A|Fire Blast}}-like attack that deals '''400''' {{D|Heat}} damage, not scaled by enemy level, and inflicts {{D|Knockdown}} and a {{D|Heat}} status effect. Rolling through the Fire Blast prevents all damage and status effects from it.

These Eximus units will release their fire wave when enemies are close to them and are capable of dealing significant damage to [[Sentinel]]s at higher levels; caution is advised when engaging them at close range.

Only [[Grineer]], [[Scaldra]], [[Rogue Arcocanid]]s and [[Vapos Shield Osprey]]s can become Arson Eximus. In [[Höllvania]], Arson Eximus are significantly more common in the [[Höllvania#Weather|Summer season]].
{{clr}}

===Bioelectric / Galvanic / Shock===
[[File:ShockEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Shock Eximus]]
'''Bioelectric''', '''Galvanic''', or '''Shock''' Eximus units release '''3''' orbs dealing '''10''' {{D|Electricity}} damage; slowly move toward Tenno within '''20m'''. The orbs lasts '''8''' seconds and can be destroyed by shooting them or killing the Eximus.

All factions can become Shock Eximus. [[Infested]] are referred to as Bioelectric. [[Rogue_Culverin#Variants|Elementa Culverins]] are referred to as Galvanic, and possess a unique mortar attack that leaves a lingering cloud of {{D|Electricity}}, which will inflict an {{D|Electricity}} status effect to anyone inside it.
{{clr}}

===Blitz / Volatile===
[[File:VolatileEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Volatile Eximus]]
'''Blitz''' or '''Volatile''' Eximus units can punch the ground to release a shockwave that travels in a forward line, dealing '''250''' {{D|Blast}} damage scaled by [[Enemy Level Scaling#Damage|enemy level]] with a guaranteed {{D|Knockdown}} and {{D|Blast}} status effect. The shockwave deals one instance of damage; getting knocked back into the shockwave's path does not deal consecutive hits.

All factions can become Blitz Eximus. [[Infested]] are referred to as Volatile.
{{clr}}

===Energy Leech / Parasitic===
[[File:EnergyLeechEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Energy Leech Eximus]]
'''Energy Leech''' or '''Parasitic''' Eximus units spawn a small purple Energy Leech Zone under visible players within line of sight, which collapses after '''3''' seconds, dealing '''50''' {{D|Magnetic}} damage and a {{D|Magnetic}} status effect to Tenno that remain in the zone when it collapses. {{D|Magnetic}} status effects from Energy Leech / Parasitic only do '''1''' tick. Sources of Magnetic status effect resistance, such as {{Arcane|Arcane Nullifier}}, will entirely negate the status effect but not the damage.

Energy Leech Eximus that are allied to Tenno will restore their energy at a rate of '''3''' units per second over '''3''' seconds upon hitting enemies.

All factions can become Energy Leech Eximus. [[Infested]] are referred to as Parasitic.

In [[Höllvania]], Energy Leech Eximus are significantly more common in the [[Höllvania#Weather|Autumn season]].
{{clr}}

===Guardian===
[[File:GuardianEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Guardian Eximus]]
'''Guardian''' Eximus units, when alerted, are surrounded by three rotating shields which are invulnerable to [[Punch Through]] and give the Guardian Eximus '''90%''' damage reduction to area of effect attacks. The shields have small gaps in between them and do not provide any protection from above or below. They also provide '''90%''' damage reduction to all attacks to their allies in range, but not for themselves or special units such as [[Demolisher]]s, [[Capture]] targets, and [[Bosses]], and the damage reduction does not stack with other nearby Guardian Eximus.

Damage reduction does not apply to {{D|Overguard}} of nearby units. However, the damage reduction against area of effect attacks <u>does</u> apply to the Overguard of the Guardian Eximus.

Only [[Corpus]], [[The Murmur|The Murmur (Necramechs)]], and [[Techrot]] ''grounded'' units can become Guardian Eximus.
{{clr}}

===Jade Light===
{{for|the Orokin execution method|Jade Light}}
[[File:JadeLightEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Jade Light Eximus]]
'''Jade Light''' Eximus release satellite lasers above up to '''2''' players that follow them for '''8''' seconds, dealing '''30''' {{D|Heat}} damage with a guaranteed {{D|Heat}} status effect every '''0.5''' seconds; with each subsequent tick doubling its damage. Heat status effects have a '''2''' second duration. On [[Defense Objects]], the laser instead deals a flat '''100''' damage per tick.

On non-Defense Objects, sequential hits by the laser deal ''double'' the damage of the previous hit. For example, getting hit by three ticks of the laser in a row will cause the first hit to deal 30 damage, the second 60 damage, and the third 120 damage, totaling 210 damage.

The laser can be destroyed by shooting the top of the beam, inflicting a {{D|Radiation}} or {{D|Confusion}} status effect on the Eximus, or killing the Eximus. The laser has health equal to '''5%''' of the eximus's {{D|Overguard}}.

In [[Höllvania]], Jade Light Eximus are significantly more common in the [[Höllvania#Weather|Spring season]].
{{clr}}

===Leech / Sanguine===
[[File:LeechEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Leech Eximus]]
'''Leech''' or '''Sanguine''' Eximus units spawn a persistent '''3''' meter spherical Health Leech Zone under visible players within line of sight before dissipating after a few seconds. Tenno in the zone are drained of '''5%''' of max health per hit at a rate of '''2''' hit per second, healing the Eximus and its allies by '''10%''' of their max health per hit. Leech Zones can spawn in mid-air. The leech zones will not damage (and thus will not trigger the heal effect) enemies that have friendly fire enabled (e.g. being afflicted with {{D|Radiation}} status effects) or companions.

All factions can become Leech Eximus. [[Infested]] are referred to as Sanguine.
{{clr}}

===Septic / Venomous===
[[File:VenomousEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Venomous Eximus]]
'''Septic''' or '''Venomous''' Eximus units emit a potent {{D|Toxin}} aura in a '''3.5''' meter radius that deals '''10''' {{D|Toxin}} damage scaled by [[Enemy Level Scaling#Damage|enemy level]] with a guaranteed {{D|Toxin}} status effect. {{D|Toxin}} status effect has a reduced duration of '''4''' seconds.

Only [[Infested]] and [[Techrot]] ''melee units'' can become Venomous Eximus. [[Rogue_Arcocanid#Variants|Elementa Arcocanids]] and [[Rogue_Culverin#Variants|Elementa Culverins]] are referred to as Septic. Septic Elementa Culverins also possess a unique mortar attack that leaves a lingering cloud of {{D|Toxin}}, which will inflict a {{D|Toxin}} status effect to anyone inside it. Interestingly, the aura of Septic Eximus units is much more vibrant than the aura of Venomous Eximus units.
{{clr}}

==Special Eximus Types==
===Prosecutors===
[[File:ToxicProsecutor.png|thumb|200px|right|Toxic Prosecutor]]
{{main|Guardsman#Prosecutor_Variant{{!}}Prosecutor}}
Unique to '''Guardsmen''' in the [[Grineer Shipyard]] tileset, these variants project an aura which grants resistance to nearly all damage types, but lowers resistance to their corresponding damage type. Unlike typical Eximus, Prosecutors have 10x base Health rather than Overguard.
{{clr}}
===Warden Eximus===
[[File:CorpusWardenEximus.png|thumb|200px|right|Corpus Warden Eximus]]
{{main|Warden}}
Unique to '''Wardens''', who are in turn exclusive to [[Rescue]] missions, these variants possess '''50%''' life leech, '''1.5x''' movement speed, and '''1.5x''' shield recharge rate. Unlike typical Eximus, Warden Eximus have +1.2 base Health rather than Overguard.
{{clr}}

